---
layout: base.njk
title: Results
permalink: results.html
---
{%- set cols = results.columns %}
{%- set tree = site.repo + '/tree/gh-pages/' %}
<h1>Results</h1>

<p class="site-lead">How well automated checkers find each test case, then and now. Each 2026 retest column sits next to its 2017 counterpart.</p>

{%- set run = results.latest %}
{%- if run %}
<p>2026 columns: run <code>{{ run.id }}</code> of {{ run.date }}, commit <a href="{{ site.repo }}/commit/{{ run.commit }}"><code>{{ run.commitShort }}</code></a>, axe-core {{ run.tools['axe-core'] }}, pa11y {{ run.tools.pa11y }} (HTML_CodeSniffer {{ run.tools.html_codesniffer }}), Chromium {{ run.browser }}. Classified by script with an AI-proposed rule mapping that is not yet human-reviewed; see the <a href="{{ '/methodology.html' | url }}#classification">methodology</a>.</p>
{%- else %}
<p><strong>The 2026 retest has not been published yet.</strong> Until it has, the AIL columns are empty.</p>
{%- endif %}

{% include "wcag-filter.njk" %}

<h2>Numbers</h2>
<ul class="site-stats">
  <li><span class="site-stat-value" data-stat-count>{{ collections.testCases.length }}</span> <span class="site-stat-label">test cases</span></li>
  {%- for e in results.engines %}
  <li><span class="site-stat-label site-stat-engine">{{ e.name }}: found or warned</span>
    <span class="site-stat-pair">
    {%- for c in cols %}{% if c.engine == e.name %}
    {%- set rate = collections.testCases | detectionRate(results.byTest, c.key) %}
      <span class="site-stat-era site-era-{{ c.era }}"><span class="site-stat-value" data-stat-col="{{ c.key }}">{{ (rate + '%') if rate !== null else '–' }}</span> <span class="site-era-label">{{ 'Then' if c.era == 'then' else 'Now' }}: {{ c.when }}, {{ c.who }}</span><span class="site-muted">{{ c.label }}{{ (' ' + c.version) if c.version }}</span></span>
    {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
    </span>
  </li>
  {%- endfor %}
</ul>
<p class="site-muted">Numbers follow the WCAG filter. Percentages count "issue found", "issue found (paid)" and "warning only" among the test cases the tool was run on. The 2017 columns cover only the GOV.UK test cases; the 2026 columns also cover the test cases added by AIL, which target criteria the tools rarely check. To compare like with like, choose "Original 2017 test cases".</p>

<details class="site-details">
  <summary>What each result means</summary>
  <p>These categories are the ones GOV.UK used in 2017, with their wording.</p>
  <h3>Positive result</h3>
  <dl>
    <dt><span class="site-result site-result-error">Issue found</span></dt><dd>The tool found the issue.</dd>
    <dt><span class="site-result site-result-error_paid">Issue found (paid)</span></dt><dd>Only the paid version of the tool found the issue.</dd>
  </dl>
  <h3>Mostly positive results</h3>
  <dl>
    <dt><span class="site-result site-result-warning">Warning only</span></dt><dd>The tool noticed the issue, but only threw up a warning.</dd>
    <dt><span class="site-result site-result-manual">User to check</span></dt><dd>The tool pointed out the potentially problematic bit of code and asked us to check ourselves whether it was an issue.</dd>
  </dl>
  <h3>Neutral result</h3>
  <dl>
    <dt><span class="site-result site-result-identified">Noticed but not a fail</span></dt><dd>The tool noticed this was potentially a problem, but didn't see it as a full-scale issue or give a warning.</dd>
  </dl>
  <h3>Negative result</h3>
  <dl>
    <dt><span class="site-result site-result-notfound">Not found</span></dt><dd>The tool didn't find the issue.</dd>
  </dl>
  <p>In 2026 the category is assigned by a script, not by hand. "Not tested" in a 2026 column means the tool did not see the barrier: the page failed to load, or the barrier is on a linked example page that the retest did not load. See the <a href="{{ '/methodology.html' | url }}#classification">methodology</a>.</p>
</details>

{%- set groups = collections.testCases | groupByCategory %}
<div class="site-table-wrap" role="region" aria-labelledby="results-caption" tabindex="0">
<table class="site-results-table">
  <caption id="results-caption">Table of results</caption>
  <colgroup><col></colgroup>
  {%- for e in results.engines %}
  <colgroup span="2"></colgroup>
  {%- endfor %}
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th scope="col" rowspan="2">Test case</th>
      {%- for e in results.engines %}
      <th scope="colgroup" colspan="2" class="site-engine-start">{{ e.name }}</th>
      {%- endfor %}
    </tr>
    <tr>
      {%- for c in cols %}
      <th scope="col" class="site-era-{{ c.era }}{{ ' site-engine-start' if c.era == 'then' }}"><span class="site-era-label">{{ 'Then' if c.era == 'then' else 'Now' }}: {{ c.when }}</span><br>{{ c.who }}<br><span class="site-muted">{{ c.label }}{{ (' ' + c.version) if c.version }}</span></th>
      {%- endfor %}
    </tr>
  </thead>
  {%- for group in groups %}
  <tbody data-wcag-group>
    <tr class="site-results-group"><th scope="rowgroup" colspan="{{ cols.length + 1 }}">{{ group.name }}</th></tr>
    {%- for item in group.items %}
    {%- set r = results.byTest[item.fileSlug] %}
    <tr data-wcag-item data-origin="{{ item.data.origin }}" data-wcag="{{ (wcag.byTest[item.fileSlug] or []) | dump | escape }}">
      <th scope="row"><a href="{{ ('/test-cases.html#' + item.fileSlug) | url }}">{{ item.data.title }}</a>{% if item.data.origin == 'ail-2026' %} <span class="site-muted">(AIL)</span>{% endif %}</th>
      {%- for c in cols %}
      {%- set v = r[c.key] if r else null %}
      {%- if v %}
      <td class="site-result-cell site-result-{{ v }}{{ ' site-engine-start' if c.era == 'then' }}" data-col="{{ c.key }}" data-value="{{ v }}">{{ results.values[v] | capitalize }}</td>
      {%- else %}
      <td class="site-result-cell{{ ' site-engine-start' if c.era == 'then' }}"><span class="site-muted">Not tested</span></td>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- endfor %}
    </tr>
    {%- endfor %}
  </tbody>
  {%- endfor %}
</table>
</div>

<h2 id="changelog">Changelog</h2>
{%- if results.runs.length %}
<p>AIL retests, newest first:</p>
<ul>
  {%- for r in results.runs %}
  <li>{{ r.date }}: run <a href="{{ tree }}data/results/ail-2026/runs/{{ r.id }}"><code>{{ r.id }}</code></a>, {{ r.pages }} test cases, commit <a href="{{ site.repo }}/commit/{{ r.commit }}"><code>{{ r.commitShort }}</code></a>{% if r.dirty %} (uncommitted changes){% endif %}. axe-core {{ r.tools['axe-core'] }}, pa11y {{ r.tools.pa11y }} with HTML_CodeSniffer {{ r.tools.html_codesniffer }}, Playwright {{ r.tools['playwright-core'] }}, Chromium {{ r.browser }}, Node.js {{ r.node }}.</li>
  {%- endfor %}
</ul>
{%- else %}
<p>AIL retests will be listed here, newest first, with the commit and tool versions used.</p>
{%- endif %}
<p>GOV.UK's changelog for 2016 to 2018, including when aXe and HTML_CodeSniffer were last retested, is on the <a href="{{ site.originalResults }}#changelog">original results page</a>.</p>

<h2>Want more detail?</h2>
<ul>
  <li>2017 results for aXe and HTML_CodeSniffer, as used here: <a href="{{ tree }}data/results/govuk-2017/results.json">data/results/govuk-2017/results.json</a></li>
  <li>2026 retest runs, with raw tool output: <a href="{{ tree }}data/results/ail-2026">data/results/ail-2026/</a></li>
  <li>Results for all 13 tools tested in 2017: <a href="{{ site.originalResults }}">original results page</a></li>
</ul>

<script src="{{ '/site-assets/wcag-filter.js' | url }}" defer></script>
<script src="{{ '/site-assets/results-stats.js' | url }}" defer></script>
